 <subsection xml:id="parking-fee-calculator">
  <title>Smart Parking Fee Calculator</title>
<p>
A downtown parking garage wants to replace its manual parking-fee system with a Python program. The 
program will ask a customer for information about their parking visit and determine how much they 
owe.
The garage has different rates depending on how long the customer parked and whether they are a garage member. The program should also 
determine whether the customer qualifies for free parking.
</p>
<p>
Create a Python program that determines a customer's parking fee based on information they provide. Your program should make decisions 
using Boolean expressions and display a personalized receipt. Be sure to format all dollar amounts in the receipt to two decimal places.
</p>

<p>Program Requirements: Ask the user for the following information and store the input into variables.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Customer name</li>
    <li>Number of hours parked</li>
    <li>Whether they are a garage member (yes or no)</li>
    <li>Whether they parked on a weekend (yes or no)</li>
  </ul>

    <table xml:id="parking-rates">
      <title>Parking Rates</title>
      <tabular>
        <row header="yes">
           <cell bottom="minor">Parking Time </cell>
          <cell bottom="minor">  Regular Customer </cell>
           <cell bottom="minor">  Member </cell>
         </row>
        <row>  
         <cell> 0.5 to 2 hours </cell>
         <cell> $5 </cell>
         <cell> $3 </cell>
        </row>
        <row>  
         <cell> More than 2 hours to 4 hours </cell>
         <cell> $10 </cell>
         <cell> $7 </cell>
        </row>
        <row>  
         <cell> More than 4 hours to 8 hours </cell>
         <cell> $18 </cell>
         <cell> $12 </cell>
        </row>
        <row>  
         <cell> More than 8 hours </cell>
         <cell> $25 </cell>
         <cell> $18 </cell>
        </row>
      </tabular>
</table>

<p>Special Rules:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Members receive a discounted rate (see table above).</li>
    <li>Parking for 30 minutes or less is free.</li>
    <li>On weekends, all customers receive an additional 20% discount.</li>
    <li>A customer who parks for more than 12 hours receives a warning that they have exceeded the recommended parking time.</li>
</ul>

